@segment  relax-10
@title    Ten-Point Relaxation
@levels   F10
@from     F1
@verbosity 3
@duration ~9m

say Now we move to the Focus 10 state. Mind awake. Body asleep.
pause 4
level F10
say As I count from one to ten, you will relax each part of your body. By the time we reach ten, your body will be completely relaxed, and your mind will remain alert and aware.
pause 4
say Let's begin.
pause 3
say First, let your jaw go limp and relax. Let the muscles and nerves in your jaw go limp and relax.
pause 6
say Now your eyelids. Let the muscles and nerves in your eyelids relax, and go limp.
pause 6
say Now your lips. Let the muscles and nerves in your lips relax. Relax easily, and go limp.
pause 6
say Now the muscles in your forehead. The muscles in your forehead. Let the muscles in your forehead relax. Go limp.
pause 6
say Now the muscles in your cheeks. Each cheek. Let them relax. Relax, and go limp. Relax.
pause 6
say Now the muscles in your scalp. The muscles in your scalp, over the top of your head. Let them relax. Relax.
pause 6
say Now the muscles in your neck. Let the muscles in your neck relax. Relax.
pause 6
say Now let the muscles in your eyes, the muscles that control your eyes. Let them relax. Relax.
pause 8
say Now let this relaxation of your head, of the muscles and nerves in your head, let it sink inward. Inward. Let it flow into your brain.
pause 6
say Let this relaxation of your head flow into your brain. Let it sink easily and deeply into your brain.
pause 8
say Feel it sinking inward, easily and calmly, until your entire brain feels more and more relaxed. More and more relaxed, as you feel the relaxation of your head sink inward, inward into the nerves of your brain, so that your brain feels relaxed.
pause 10
say Now that your brain feels and understands this relaxation, as I count to ten, let it flow from the brain. Let it flow from the brain into every part of your physical body.
pause 6
say Into your toes, into your feet, into your legs, into your hips. Into your lower body, into your upper body, into your back, into your fingers, into your hands, into your arms, into your shoulders.
pause 6
say Let it flow into these parts as I guide you in the count to the ten state. I'm going to count now.
pause 4
say Four. Look with your closed eyes at your feet and your toes. Your brain tells the muscles and nerves in each foot and each toe to relax, let go, sleep.
pause 10
say Five. Look with your closed eyes at your legs, at each leg, from your hip down to your foot. Your brain tells each leg to relax. Let go. Sleep.
pause 10
say Six. Look with your closed eyes at your hips, at each hip. Your brain tells each hip, the muscles and nerves in each hip, to relax, let go. Sleep.
pause 10
say Seven. Look with your closed eyes at your lower body. Your abdomen down to your hips, your kidneys, your liver, your stomach, your intestines, your genitals. Your brain tells all of these parts in your lower body to relax. Let go. Sleep.
pause 10
say Eight. Look with your closed eyes at your upper body. Your chest, your heart, your lungs, your diaphragm. Your brain tells these parts of your body to relax, let go, sleep.
pause 10
say Nine. Look with your closed eyes up and down your back. The muscles and nerves in your back. Your brain tells your back, up and down your back, the muscles and nerves in your back, to relax. Let go. Sleep.
pause 10
say Ten. Look with your closed eyes at your upper body. Your arms, your hands, your fingers, your shoulders. Your brain tells all of these parts to relax, let go, sleep.
pause 8
say Ten. Ten. Ten.
pause 6
say Relax, and be calm and comfortable in Focus 10. The ten state, where your mind is bright and alert.
pause 5
say Your physical body is deeply, calmly, and comfortably asleep.
pause 5
say Mind awake. Body asleep.
pause 10
